    "notes": "Zebrasoma flavescens, fable-v2: deep, nearly round disc (max body depth 0.096 m = 57 percent of the 0.168 m SL, up from 43 percent in fable-v1), deepest just behind the pectoral. Convex nape, steep (about 60 degree) concave forehead that drops from the dorsal-fin origin into a distinct proboscis-like snout: the snout root (where the section depth falls under 30 percent of the maximum) sits 0.017 m (10 percent SL) behind the tip, the snout axis dips 0.0135 m below the body axis, the small terminal mouth is at the tip, and the eye is high on the forehead 0.026 m behind the tip. Short narrow peduncle (12 percent SL deep) with a white scalpel, truncate yellow tail, tall dorsal and anal sails peaking mid-body (14.6 and 11.6 percent SL). Lateral width kept at 0.023 m so the disc reads volumetric from top and front. Proportions from FishBase description and Commons photographs (proportion only).",
